            <div xml:id="d729">

                <pb facs="0759" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg751"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/409: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Luxemburg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Waller</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-06-28T19:00:00-04:00">June 28, 1938—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. Your 16, June 27, noon. Invitations to attend the Evian meeting were extended
                    only to those countries which offered some reasonable possibility of accepting a
                    substantial number of immigrants. Inasmuch as Luxemburg can not be considered in
                    that category we consider it impracticable to extend an invitation, at least at
                    the present stage of proceedings.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
